# --- Cloud (default) ------------------------------------------------------

# Cloud discovery is pinned to https://control.kumiho.cloud. Authentication,
# refresh, discovery, and assigned-region routing are owned by the Python SDK.
# Do not put a Cloud token or custom control-plane/tenant route in this plugin
# file. Prefer a persistent KUMIHO_AUTH_TOKEN in the OS/user or trusted host
# environment before Claude starts. Without one, use `kumiho-auth login` or
# `kumiho-cli login`; all hosts share the SDK-owned ~/.kumiho credential store.
# The plugin never saves or copies the token.

# --- Self-hosted Community Edition (CE) -----------------------------------
# Opt-in. When enabled, the launcher skips control-plane discovery and cloud
# auth and talks to a local kumiho-server CE over gRPC. No Cloud token is used
# in this mode. See README "Self-hosted (Community Edition)".

# Enable CE mode:
# KUMIHO_CLAUDE_MODE=ce

# Override the CE gRPC endpoint (default 127.0.0.1:9190). Setting this alone
# also enables CE mode:
# KUMIHO_CLAUDE_SERVER_ENDPOINT=127.0.0.1:9190

# CE working-memory Redis (default redis://127.0.0.1:6379):
# UPSTASH_REDIS_URL=redis://127.0.0.1:6379

# Point summarization at a local/self-hosted LLM (OpenAI-compatible):
# KUMIHO_LLM_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1

